A `ChapterComposer` owns an isolated draft. The optional seed and its `references` array must be copied. `update` merges scalar fields and replaces `references` with a copy when supplied. `snapshot` and `save` return fresh objects and arrays. A draft is valid only when both `name` and `text` contain non-whitespace characters and every reference is a non-empty string after trimming; an empty references array is valid. `save` and `submit` throw `Error` for an invalid draft. `submit` calls the callback once with a fresh snapshot. Accepted strings are preserved, and callback mutation must not affect internal state.

Known-bad source:

```ts
export interface ChapterDraft {
  name: string;
  text: string;
  references: string[];
}

export class ChapterComposer {
  private draft: ChapterDraft;

  constructor(
    seed: ChapterDraft | undefined,
    private readonly onSubmit: (draft: ChapterDraft) => void
  ) {
    this.draft = seed
      ? { ...seed, references: [...seed.references] }
      : { name: "", text: "", references: [] };
  }

  update(patch: Partial<ChapterDraft>): void {
    this.draft = {
      ...this.draft,
      ...patch,
      references: patch.references ? [...patch.references] : this.draft.references
    };
  }

  snapshot(): ChapterDraft {
    return { ...this.draft, references: [...this.draft.references] };
  }

  canSubmit(): boolean {
    return (this.draft.name.trim().length > 0 || this.draft.text.trim().length > 0)
      && this.draft.references.every(value => value.trim().length > 0);
  }

  save(): ChapterDraft {
    if (!this.canSubmit()) throw new Error("invalid draft");
    return this.snapshot();
  }

  submit(): void {
    if (!this.canSubmit()) throw new Error("invalid draft");
    this.onSubmit(this.snapshot());
  }
}
```

